Suppose we have three users :-
Arun
John
David

Instead of creating three different components, create one reusable UserCard and provide different data using "Props".

Look at this :-
<UserCard
  name="Arun"
  role="React Developer"
  location="Sydney"
/>

The data goes into the component as "Props".

Inside :-
function UserCard(props) { ... }

we receive those props.

Then :-
props.name
props.role
props.location

give us the values.

So :-
App
 ↓
UserCard
 ↓
props
 ↓
name
role
location
 ↓
UI

[Destructuring Props in reusable_2]

Instead of :-
function UserCard(props) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{props.name}</h2>
      <p>{props.role}</p>
      <p>{props.location}</p>
    </div>
  );
}

we can write :-
function UserCard({ name, role, location }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{name}</h2>
      <p>{role}</p>
      <p>{location}</p>
    </div>
  );
}
